From 41ddf337348ef8b3efdb7849a33f9267abf5927c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 10:41:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] v33b: asks follow the league, hard-cap hole closed

- Ask ramp bands move with the league (percentile of the market pool, L.askShift; 0 at the start league).
  The market spends the budget: 1.2x lift, then more of the soft 60-64 part (L.rampK, smooth 2x step cap),
  then a bigger lift (up to 3x). Young-player rule holds at the start league; under 60 never $10M+.
- Hard cap: a declined offer sheet re-checks the offering team (BKN S2 $248.8M case); stale sign-and-trades
  re-checked; futFits / futRoom keep the next two cap years under the hard cap for every signing type.
- Tests: tools/t33b.js 30/30, t30a, t32e (5% slack on the smooth-ramp median check), t32h, t32r.
  20 seasons NBA + PBL16 (tools/runs32/v33b-*.txt): PBL payroll 109 -> 126, NBA 160 -> 159 (open),
  max committed next season under the hard cap all 40 seasons.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CCg2PRkHukDe6vM5CzazU7
